    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408">

                <pb facs="0451" n="1185" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1185"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Taylor.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-05"><hi rendition="#italic">June 5,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 338.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 357, of the 20th ultimo, in
                    relation to the <hi rendition="#italic">Alliança</hi> incident, was duly
                    received, and I have laid before the President the note of his excellency the
                    minister of state, of the 16th ultimo, conveying the disavowal by His Majesty’s
                    Government of the act of the temporary commander of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Venadito</hi> in firing upon the <hi rendition="#italic">Alliança</hi> and
                    the assurance that instructions have been sent to Spanish naval commanders in
                    order to avoid the repetition of any such occurrence.</p>
                <p>I am directed by the President to instruct you that, without conceding that the
                    exact location of the <hi rendition="#italic">Alliança</hi> at the time the shot
                    was fired can be considered a controlling circumstance, this communication of
                    His Majesty’s Government is accepted as a sufficient and satisfactory
                    explanation of the incident.</p>
                <p>You will add an expression of the President’s high appreciation of the friendly
                    tenor of the Duke of Tetuan’s note.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
